2026-09-15T19:46Z claude note Observed tonight on padme, v0.4.16, Zotero 10.0.2, three libraries. The panel read "Stored or linked file unavailable 13 699" against "Indexed and up to date 2", and both the author and this session first read it as a defect. It was not: `storage/` held 688 attachment folders at 19:39 and 1 285 at 19:43, growing ~1 000 files/minute — the census had classified a library whose files were ~9 % present. The reconciliation line said "last full pass, 3 min 43 s ago" and was correct. An age in minutes does not warn that the data behind it is 95 % obsolete.
